(in-ns 'go.math.big.internal.asmgen) (go/file "mul.go" :imports [])


^{:go/end 16} (go/func mulAddVWW "mulAddVWW generates mulAddVWW, which does z, c = x*m + a.\n" [^{:tag (* Asm)} a]
  (let [f (.Func a "func mulAddVWW(z, x []Word, m, a Word) (c Word)")]

    (when (.Valid (.AltCarry a))
      (addMulVirtualCarry f 0)
      (return))

    (addMul f "" "x" 0)))




^{:go/end 43} (go/func addMulVVWW "addMulVVWW generates addMulVVWW which does z, c = x + y*m + a.\n(A more pedantic name would be addMulAddVVWW.)\n" [^{:tag (* Asm)} a]
  (let [f (.Func a "func addMulVVWW(z, x, y []Word, m, a Word) (c Word)")]

    ;; If the architecture has virtual carries, emit that version unconditionally.
    (when (.Valid (.AltCarry a))
      (addMulVirtualCarry f 1)
      (return))


    ;; If the architecture optionally has two carries, test and emit both versions.
    (when (.JmpEnable a OptionAltCarry "altcarry")
      (let [regs (.RegsUsed a)]
        (addMul f "x" "y" 1)
        (.Label a "altcarry")
        (.SetOption a OptionAltCarry true)
        (.SetRegsUsed a regs)
        (addMulAlt f)
        (.SetOption a OptionAltCarry false)
        (return)))


    ;; Otherwise emit the one-carry form.
    (addMul f "x" "y" 1)))





































































































































^{:go/end 234} (go/func addMul "Computing z = addsrc + m*mulsrc + a, we need:\n\n\tfor i := range z {\n\t\tlo, hi := m * mulsrc[i]\n\t\tlo, carry = bits.Add(lo, a, 0)\n\t\tlo, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo, addsrc[i], 0)\n\t\tz[i] = lo\n\t\ta = hi + carry + carryAlt  // cannot overflow\n\t}\n\nThe final addition cannot overflow because after processing N words,\nthe maximum possible value is (for a 64-bit system):\n\n\t  (2**64N - 1) + (2**64 - 1)*(2**64N - 1) + (2**64 - 1)\n\t= (2**64)*(2**64N - 1) + (2**64 - 1)\n\t= 2**64(N+1) - 1,\n\nwhich fits in N+1 words (the high order one being the new value of a).\n\n(For example, with 3 decimal words, 999 + 9*999 + 9 = 999*10 + 9 = 9999.)\n\nIf we unroll the loop a bit, then we can chain the carries in two passes.\nConsider:\n\n\tlo0, hi0 := m * mulsrc[i]\n\tlo0, carry = bits.Add(lo0, a, 0)\n\tlo0, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo0, addsrc[i], 0)\n\tz[i] = lo0\n\ta = hi + carry + carryAlt // cannot overflow\n\n\tlo1, hi1 := m * mulsrc[i]\n\tlo1, carry = bits.Add(lo1, a, 0)\n\tlo1, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo1, addsrc[i], 0)\n\tz[i] = lo1\n\ta = hi + carry + carryAlt // cannot overflow\n\n\tlo2, hi2 := m * mulsrc[i]\n\tlo2, carry = bits.Add(lo2, a, 0)\n\tlo2, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo2, addsrc[i], 0)\n\tz[i] = lo2\n\ta = hi + carry + carryAlt // cannot overflow\n\n\tlo3, hi3 := m * mulsrc[i]\n\tlo3, carry = bits.Add(lo3, a, 0)\n\tlo3, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo3, addsrc[i], 0)\n\tz[i] = lo3\n\ta = hi + carry + carryAlt // cannot overflow\n\nThere are three ways we can optimize this sequence.\n\n(1) Reordering, we can chain carries so that we can use one hardware carry flag\nbut amortize the cost of saving and restoring it across multiple instructions:\n\n\t// multiply\n\tlo0, hi0 := m * mulsrc[i]\n\tlo1, hi1 := m * mulsrc[i+1]\n\tlo2, hi2 := m * mulsrc[i+2]\n\tlo3, hi3 := m * mulsrc[i+3]\n\n\tlo0, carry = bits.Add(lo0, a, 0)\n\tlo1, carry = bits.Add(lo1, hi0, carry)\n\tlo2, carry = bits.Add(lo2, hi1, carry)\n\tlo3, carry = bits.Add(lo3, hi2, carry)\n\ta = hi3 + carry // cannot overflow\n\n\t// add\n\tlo0, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo0, addsrc[i], 0)\n\tlo1, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo1, addsrc[i+1], carryAlt)\n\tlo2, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo2, addsrc[i+2], carryAlt)\n\tlo3, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo3, addrsc[i+3], carryAlt)\n\ta = a + carryAlt // cannot overflow\n\n\tz[i] = lo0\n\tz[i+1] = lo1\n\tz[i+2] = lo2\n\tz[i+3] = lo3\n\naddMul takes this approach, using the hardware carry flag\nfirst for carry and then for carryAlt.\n\n(2) addMulAlt assumes there are two hardware carry flags available.\nIt dedicates one each to carry and carryAlt, so that a multi-block\nunrolling can keep the flags in hardware across all the blocks.\nSo even if the block size is 1, the code can do:\n\n\t// multiply and add\n\tlo0, hi0 := m * mulsrc[i]\n\tlo0, carry = bits.Add(lo0, a, 0)\n\tlo0, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo0, addsrc[i], 0)\n\tz[i] = lo0\n\n\tlo1, hi1 := m * mulsrc[i+1]\n\tlo1, carry = bits.Add(lo1, hi0, carry)\n\tlo1, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo1, addsrc[i+1], carryAlt)\n\tz[i+1] = lo1\n\n\tlo2, hi2 := m * mulsrc[i+2]\n\tlo2, carry = bits.Add(lo2, hi1, carry)\n\tlo2, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo2, addsrc[i+2], carryAlt)\n\tz[i+2] = lo2\n\n\tlo3, hi3 := m * mulsrc[i+3]\n\tlo3, carry = bits.Add(lo3, hi2, carry)\n\tlo3, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo3, addrsc[i+3], carryAlt)\n\tz[i+3] = lo2\n\n\ta = hi3 + carry + carryAlt // cannot overflow\n\n(3) addMulVirtualCarry optimizes for systems with explicitly computed carry bits\n(loong64, mips, riscv64), cutting the number of actual instructions almost by half.\nLook again at the original word-at-a-time version:\n\n\tlo1, hi1 := m * mulsrc[i]\n\tlo1, carry = bits.Add(lo1, a, 0)\n\tlo1, carryAlt = bits.Add(lo1, addsrc[i], 0)\n\tz[i] = lo1\n\ta = hi + carry + carryAlt // cannot overflow\n\nAlthough it uses four adds per word, those are cheap adds: the two bits.Add adds\nuse two instructions each (ADD+SLTU) and the final + adds only use one ADD each,\nfor a total of 6 instructions per word. In contrast, the middle stanzas in (2) use\nonly two “adds” per word, but these are SetCarry|UseCarry adds, which compile to\nfive instruction each, for a total of 10 instructions per word. So the word-at-a-time\nloop is actually better. And we can reorder things slightly to use only a single carry bit:\n\n\tlo1, hi1 := m * mulsrc[i]\n\tlo1, carry = bits.Add(lo1, a, 0)\n\ta = hi + carry\n\tlo1, carry = bits.Add(lo1, addsrc[i], 0)\n\ta = a + carry\n\tz[i] = lo1\n" [^{:tag (* Func)} f ^string addsrc ^string mulsrc ^int mulIndex]
  (let [a (.-Asm f)
      ^{:line 178} mh HintNone]
    (when (and (== (.-Arch a) Arch386) (!= addsrc ""))
      (set! mh HintMemOK)) ; too few registers otherwise

    (let [m (.ArgHint f "m" mh)
        ^{:line 183} c (.Arg f "a")
        ^{:line 184} n (.Arg f "z_len")

        ^{:line 186} p (.Pipe f)]
      (when (!= addsrc "")
        (.SetHint p addsrc HintMemOK))

      (.SetHint p mulsrc HintMulSrc)
      (let [unroll (lit (slice int) 1 4)]
        (switch (.-Arch a)
          (case [Arch386]
            (set! unroll (lit (slice int) 1))) ; too few registers
          (case [ArchARM]
            (.SetMaxColumns p 2)) ; too few registers (but more than 386)
          (case [ArchARM64]
            (set! unroll (lit (slice int) 1 8)))) ; 5% speedup on c4as16


        ;; See the large comment above for an explanation of the code being generated.
        ;; This is optimization strategy 1.
        (.Start p n (spread unroll))
        (.Loop p ^{:go/end 230} (fn [^{:tag (slice (slice Reg))} in ^{:tag (slice (slice Reg))} out]
            (.Comment a "multiply")
            (let [prev c
                ^{:line 207} flag SetCarry]
              (range [i x (aget in mulIndex)]
                (let [hi (.RegHint a HintMulHi)]
                  (.MulWide a m x x hi)
                  (.Add a prev x x flag)
                  (set! flag (bit-or UseCarry SetCarry))
                  (when (!= prev c)
                    (.Free a prev))

                  (aset (aget out 0) i x)
                  (set! prev hi)))

              (.Add a (.Imm a 0) prev c (bit-or UseCarry SmashCarry))
              (when (!= addsrc "")
                (.Comment a "add")
                (let [flag SetCarry]
                  (range [i x (aget in 0)]
                    (.Add a x (aget (aget out 0) i) (aget (aget out 0) i) flag)
                    (set! flag (bit-or UseCarry SetCarry)))

                  (.Add a (.Imm a 0) c c (bit-or UseCarry SmashCarry))))

              (.StoreN p out))))


        (.StoreArg f c "c")
        (.Ret a)))))


^{:go/end 291} (go/func addMulAlt [^{:tag (* Func)} f]
  (let [a (.-Asm f)
      ^{:line 238} m (.ArgHint f "m" HintMulSrc)
      ^{:line 239} c (.Arg f "a")
      ^{:line 240} n (.Arg f "z_len")

      ;; On amd64, we need a non-immediate for the AtUnrollEnd adds.
      ^{:line 243} r0 (.ZR a)]
    (when (not (.Valid r0))
      (set! r0 (.Reg a))
      (.Mov a (.Imm a 0) r0))


    (let [p (.Pipe f)]
      (.SetLabel p "alt")
      (.SetHint p "x" HintMemOK)
      (.SetHint p "y" HintMemOK)
      (when (== (.-Arch a) ArchAMD64)
        (.SetMaxColumns p 2))


      ;; See the large comment above for an explanation of the code being generated.
      ;; This is optimization strategy (2).
      (let [^Reg hi (zero Reg)
          ^{:line 260} prev c]
        (.Start p n 1 8)
        (.AtUnrollStart p ^{:go/end 267} (fn []
            (.Comment a "multiply and add")
            (.ClearCarry a (bit-or AddCarry AltCarry))
            (.ClearCarry a AddCarry)
            (set! hi (.Reg a))))

        (.AtUnrollEnd p ^{:go/end 272} (fn []
            (.Add a r0 prev c (bit-or UseCarry SmashCarry))
            (.Add a r0 c c (bit-or UseCarry SmashCarry AltCarry))
            (set! prev c)))

        (.Loop p ^{:go/end 287} (fn [^{:tag (slice (slice Reg))} in ^{:tag (slice (slice Reg))} out]
            (range [i y (aget in 1)]
              (let [x (aget (aget in 0) i)
                  ^{:line 276} lo y]
                (when (.IsMem lo)
                  (set! lo (.Reg a)))

                (.MulWide a m y lo hi)
                (.Add a prev lo lo (bit-or UseCarry SetCarry))
                (.Add a x lo lo (bit-or UseCarry SetCarry AltCarry))
                (aset (aget out 0) i lo)
                (set! (values prev hi) (values hi prev))))

            (.StoreN p out)))


        (.StoreArg f c "c")
        (.Ret a)))))


^{:go/end 320} (go/func addMulVirtualCarry [^{:tag (* Func)} f ^int mulIndex]
  (let [a (.-Asm f)
      ^{:line 295} m (.Arg f "m")
      ^{:line 296} c (.Arg f "a")
      ^{:line 297} n (.Arg f "z_len")

      ;; See the large comment above for an explanation of the code being generated.
      ;; This is optimization strategy (3).
      ^{:line 301} p (.Pipe f)]
    (.Start p n 1 4)
    (.Loop p ^{:go/end 317} (fn [^{:tag (slice (slice Reg))} in ^{:tag (slice (slice Reg))} out]
        (.Comment a "synthetic carry, one column at a time")
        (let [(values lo hi) (values (.Reg a) (.Reg a))]
          (range [i x (aget in mulIndex)]
            (.MulWide a m x lo hi)
            (when (== mulIndex 1)
              (.Add a (aget (aget in 0) i) lo lo SetCarry)
              (.Add a (.Imm a 0) hi hi (bit-or UseCarry SmashCarry)))

            (.Add a c lo x SetCarry)
            (.Add a (.Imm a 0) hi c (bit-or UseCarry SmashCarry))
            (aset (aget out 0) i x))

          (.StoreN p out))))

    (.StoreArg f c "c")
    (.Ret a)))
